        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <article class="faq-item">
            <h3>What does Tectori do?</h3>
            <p>
              Tectori provides founder-led cloud architecture and operations,
              cybersecurity, compliance and risk management, IT operations,
              fractional IT and security leadership, and governed AI consulting.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <h3>Who does Tectori serve?</h3>
            <p>
              Tectori is designed for banks, credit unions, healthcare
              organizations, regulated businesses, and growing companies that
              need technology to support customer diligence, enterprise
              expectations, or regulatory scrutiny.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <h3>What is audit-ready IT?</h3>
            <p>
              Audit-ready IT connects regulatory and business requirements to
              architecture decisions, policies, controls, ownership,
              documentation, testing, and evidence produced during normal
              operation. It is not a promise that every audit will produce a
              particular result.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <h3>How does Tectori approach AI governance?</h3>
            <p>
              Tectori treats AI governance as an operating system with approved
              use cases, accountable owners, data boundaries, human review,
              monitoring, incident handling, change control, and retained
              decision records.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is Tectori a large consulting firm?</h3>
            <p>
              No. Tectori is a founder-led practice. Clients work directly
              with Jonathan Bowker, the practitioner responsible for
              recommendations, design, and delivery.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Tectori sell software?</h3>
            <p>
              Tectori builds and maintains several products as separate
              brands, including Fortivra, Compliance Compass, MailSweep,
              FileIQ, Architect Copilot, and Lumenwatch. They are working
              reference implementations of the standards behind Tectori's
              consulting work and are not offered for sale at this time.
              Tectori also publishes free, open source tools on GitHub,
              including Ops Toolkit, Security Program Templates, and Email
              Evidence Tools.
            </p>
          </article>
